 "note_en": "The literary frame 以…为… means \"to take … as…,\" \"to make … the basis\": 以慢为主 \"slowness above all.\" Its sibling is 以 meaning \"by means of\": 以柔克刚 \"use softness to overcome hardness.\" These come from Classical Chinese and sound like proverbs in modern speech; 以公园为家 \"to treat the park as one's home\" is built the same way.",
